   "observation": "B=200 carries the CHEAP signature 8,1,8,8,3|8,1,8,8,3 and is still the most expensive plan at R=200, because it is vector width 4.",
   "consequence": "The signature does NOT protect against the width penalty. The two axes are independent, so the order of operations matters: filter by v2(B)+v2(L) FIRST, then rank by signature. Ranking by signature first leads straight to the worst batch.",
   "also": "B=100 carries the dear signature AND width 4, so it is bad twice over."
